# Allowlist .gitignore.
#
# Rule: deny everything, then re-include named public paths. A denylist
# leaks the manuscript the first time somebody adds a file, and a leak in a
# public history cannot be undone by deleting the file later.
#
# Anything not named below is private. To publish a new file, add one line
# here and re-run the split audit.

/*

# --- public root files ---------------------------------------------------
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/README.md
!/CITATION.cff
!/LICENSE
!/pyproject.toml
!/main.py
!/requirements.txt
!/requirements-lock.txt
!/requirements-gui.txt

# --- public directories --------------------------------------------------
!/src/
!/DATA/
!/results/
!/tests/

# --- scripts: only named computation scripts are published ---------------
!/scripts/
/scripts/*
!/scripts/record_environment.py
!/scripts/build_data.py
!/scripts/run_experiments.py
!/scripts/make_figures.py
!/scripts/make_tables.py
!/scripts/make_explorer.py
!/scripts/check_submission.py

# --- never published, wherever they appear -------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
*.docx
*.doc
*.tex
*.bib
*.bbl
*.aux
*.synctex.gz
*.zip
*.pdf
*.eps
.env
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
secrets.*

# --- the one published exception: figures are computation output ---------
# The PNG is what the journal receives; the PDF is the vector master kept
# for re-export; captions.md holds each caption in the wording the
# manuscript uses, beside the code that drew the figure so the two cannot
# drift. EPS is no longer produced - Mathematics takes raster at 600 dpi.
!/results/figures/*.png
!/results/figures/*.pdf
!/results/figures/captions.md

# The generated LaTeX tables are deliberately NOT published: *.tex is the
# manuscript's own extension and the manuscript is not public until it is
# accepted. Nothing is lost - the tables are derived from published CSVs by
# a published script, so anyone can rebuild them with one command. The
# Markdown copies are published, and carry the same numbers.
#
# The interactive appendix is published: it is the supplementary material
# the paper points at, and it has to work from a downloaded copy with no
# network, so it is one self-contained file.
!/results/explorer.html
